"""
Ship compartment: a moist-air space behind weather-exposed bulkheads, with both film
coefficients computed rather than assumed.

This is `HVACComponents.Components.MultiportLumpedRoom` with its two fixed-`U`
`ThermalConductor`s replaced by the convection factors in this package: `InternalConvection`
on the room side, which knows whether a surface is a deck, a deckhead or a bulkhead and
which way the heat is flowing, and `ExternalConvection` on the weather side, which reads
the wind.

That substitution is the point. A building's outside film coefficient is near enough
constant to be a parameter; a ship's is not. A deckhouse alongside in still air sees about
5 W/(m²·K), and the same deckhouse steaming at 8 m/s into a 12 m/s headwind sees about
75 — the hull carries its own weather with it. Feeding `ApparentSpeedXY`'s output into
`WindVector_*` makes the compartment's heat loss follow the ship's speed and heading.

Structure, per surface `i` of `N_surf`:

```
volume  ─ inner[i] ─ wall.heatPort_a[i] ═ wall.heatPort_b[i] ─ outer[i] ─ heatPorts[i]
(air)     (natural)   (inner face)        (outer face)         (wind)     (ambient)
```

The wall is `ThreeTempWall1D`: `N_surf` independent parallel surfaces, each resolved
through its thickness as an inner face, an outer face and a mid-plane carrying the
thermal mass. The air volume is a `MultiportVolume` on moist-air media, so the compartment
tracks humidity as well as temperature — a compartment's dew point is what decides whether
its bulkheads sweat.

`N_flow` fluid ports take HVAC ducts. `QSensPort` and `QLatPort` take sensible and latent
gains (crew, galley, machinery) as heat flows.

Notes on the library components underneath:

- `ThreeTempWall1D.m_wall` is documented as "the total wall mass shared by all N surfaces",
  but each surface's energy balance divides by the whole of `cp_wall * m_wall`, so N
  surfaces carry N times that mass. This component takes `rho_wall` and computes the
  per-surface mass `rho_wall * d_wall * A_wall`, which is what makes the wall's thermal
  mass come out right.
- All `N_surf` surfaces share one area, orientation and construction, as they do in
  `MultiportLumpedRoom`. A compartment with genuinely different surfaces — a sunlit
  deckhead over insulated bulkheads — wants one instance per group, joined through their
  fluid ports.
- The weather side takes plain ambient air. For a surface that also sees the sun and the
  sky, connect `ConvRadSunWall` to `heatPorts[i]` instead of an ambient boundary; it
  carries its own `ExternalConvection`, so set this component's surfaces to the shaded
  ones.
"""
component ShipCompartment
  "Number of moist-air fluid ports (HVAC ducts)"
  structural parameter N_flow::Integer
  "Number of weather-exposed surfaces"
  structural parameter N_surf::Integer

  "Compartment air volume [m³]"
  parameter V_tot::Real
  "Moist-air medium data object"
  parameter medium_data::HVACComponents.MediaModels.AbstractMoistAirMedium = HVACComponents.moistair
  "Initial air pressure [Pa]"
  parameter p_start::Pressure = 101325
  "Initial air temperature [K]"
  parameter T_start::Temperature = 293.15
  "Initial water-vapour mass fraction [-]"
  parameter Xi_start::Real = 0.007

  "Thermal conductivity of the bulkhead construction [W/(m·K)]"
  parameter lambda_wall::ThermalConductivity = 0.045
  "Specific heat capacity of the bulkhead construction [J/(kg·K)]"
  parameter cp_wall::SpecificHeatCapacity = 840
  "Density of the bulkhead construction [kg/m³]"
  parameter rho_wall::Density = 120
  "Bulkhead thickness [m]"
  parameter d_wall::Length = 0.05
  "Area of one surface [m²]"
  parameter A_wall::Area
  "Initial bulkhead temperature [K]"
  parameter T_wall_start::Temperature = 293.15

  "Orientation of the room-side surfaces, for the natural-convection coefficient"
  structural parameter inner_wall_type::WallType = WallType.Wall()
  "Outward normal of the weather-side surfaces"
  parameter Norm::Real[3] = [0, -1, 0]

  "Apparent wind over the surfaces, east component — points the way the wind travels [m/s]"
  WindVector_x = RealInput()
  "Apparent wind, north component [m/s]"
  WindVector_y = RealInput()
  "Apparent wind, up component [m/s]"
  WindVector_z = RealInput()

  "HVAC duct connections"
  ports = [HVACComponents.MoistAirFluidPort() for i in 1:N_flow]
  "Ambient air on the weather side of each surface"
  heatPorts = [HeatPort() for i in 1:N_surf]
  "Sensible gains into the compartment air"
  QSensPort = HeatPort()
  "Latent gains into the compartment air"
  QLatPort = HeatPort()

  volume = HVACComponents.Components.MultiportVolume(
    N_ports = N_flow,
    N_heat = N_surf + 1,
    V_tot = V_tot,
    medium_data = medium_data,
    p_start = p_start,
    T_start = T_start,
    Xi_start = Xi_start
  )

  wall = HVACComponents.Components.ThreeTempWall1D(
    N = N_surf,
    lambda_wall = lambda_wall,
    cp_wall = cp_wall,
    d_wall = d_wall,
    A_wall = A_wall,
    m_wall = rho_wall * d_wall * A_wall,
    T_start_inner = T_wall_start,
    T_start_outer = T_wall_start
  )

  inner = [InternalConvection(Surf = A_wall, wall_type = inner_wall_type) for i in 1:N_surf]
  outer = [ExternalConvection(Surf = A_wall, Norm = Norm) for i in 1:N_surf]

  "Room-side film coefficient [W/(m²·K)]"
  variable h_inner::CoefficientOfHeatTransfer
  "Weather-side film coefficient [W/(m²·K)]"
  variable h_outer::CoefficientOfHeatTransfer
  "Compartment air temperature [K]"
  variable T_air::Temperature
relations
  for i in 1:N_flow
    connect(ports[i], volume.ports[i])
  end

  connect(QSensPort, volume.heatPorts[N_surf + 1])
  connect(QLatPort, volume.QLatPort)

  for i in 1:N_surf
    connect(volume.heatPorts[i], inner[i].fluid)
    connect(inner[i].solid, wall.heatPort_a[i])
    connect(wall.heatPort_b[i], outer[i].solid)
    connect(outer[i].fluid, heatPorts[i])
    connect(WindVector_x, outer[i].WindVector_x)
    connect(WindVector_y, outer[i].WindVector_y)
    connect(WindVector_z, outer[i].WindVector_z)
  end

  # The surfaces are identical, so surface 1 reports for all of them.
  h_inner = inner[1].h
  h_outer = outer[1].h
  T_air = volume.medium.T
end
